# Code Review Guidelines

## Always check

- Every PHP file starts with `declare(strict_types=1)`
- Services and DTOs use `final readonly class`
- No string concatenation in Doctrine/DBAL queries (SQL injection)
- No `|raw` on user-controlled variables in Twig (XSS)
- Database migrations are additive-only (no column drops without migration plan)
- `NOT NULL` columns added with a `DEFAULT` value (or in two migrations)
- New API endpoints have `security` attribute on each operation
- New Doctrine associations have explicit `onDelete` on `JoinColumn`
- Cascade configured at every level for multi-level relationships
- Messenger messages carry IDs, not entity objects
- File uploads validated by content (`getMimeType()`), not extension
- No passwords, tokens, or PII in logger context arrays
- Error responses don't expose internal exception messages (`$e->getMessage()`)
- `json_decode()` / `json_encode()` always use `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR`

## Style

- Use early returns (guard clauses). Never nest conditionals beyond 1 level
- Use `match` expressions over `switch` for value mapping
- Use `str_contains()` / `str_starts_with()` instead of `strpos()`
- Explicit variable names, no abbreviations
- Structured logging with context arrays, not string interpolation

## Skip

- Files under `migrations/` (auto-generated by Doctrine; review the SQL, not the PHP structure)
- Files under `vendor/` and `node_modules/`
- Lock files (`composer.lock`, `package-lock.json`)
- Test fixtures data (not test logic)
